.TH CUTTING-GARDEN 1
.SH NAME
cutting-garden, cg - capture, restore, diff, and traverse trees via URI-scheme plugins
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cutting-garden
[\fIflags\fR]
\fIsubcommand\fR
[\fIargs\fR]
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B capture
capture one or more directory trees into madder's blob stores
.TP
.B diff
compare a directory tree against a capture receipt
.TP
.B failures
inspect a capture failure receipt
.TP
.B fmt-organize
regenerate an organize document in place from its envelope
.TP
.B health
report registered plugins and their capabilities
.TP
.B list
list the child nodes of a traversable plugin URI
.TP
.B mcp
serve traversable plugin endpoints over the Model Context Protocol
.TP
.B organize
reorganize a plugin's nodes by editing a faceted document
.TP
.B restore
restore a captured tree from a receipt blob
.TP
.B serve
receive files over the LocalSend protocol as captures
.TP
.B serve-mcp
serve the MCP server to many sessions over one unix socket
.TP
.B version
print the build version and commit
.SH SEE ALSO
cutting-garden-capture(1), cutting-garden-diff(1), cutting-garden-failures(1), cutting-garden-fmt-organize(1), cutting-garden-health(1), cutting-garden-list(1), cutting-garden-mcp(1), cutting-garden-organize(1), cutting-garden-restore(1), cutting-garden-serve(1), cutting-garden-serve-mcp(1), cutting-garden-version(1)
